  "conclusions": [
    "The sole JSX attribute is on the outer SVG whose source viewBox otherwise uses meet; none makes its pixel-to-box mapping agree with the HTML image before sourceScale cancellation.",
    "Grounded hulls short-circuit the condition. Classic profile and all classic variants have the same 1536x1024 canvas, so sourceScale remains absent and the old SVG setting is preserved.",
    "The actual inner image getScreenCTM is collected beside painted anchors in the existing browser evaluation; no additional evaluation, wait, timer, or playback clock is introduced.",
    "The oracle checks actual image identity/dimensions, finite CTM, isotropic orthogonal pixel axes, and both calibrated anchors. It does not reject the intended carrier-facing reflection.",
    "Four ship-capable families must expose at least one actual cloaked two-layer mixture with differing decoded canvases; a same-canvas ventral-to-ventral blend alone cannot qualify the correction.",
    "The prior classic scenario functions and shared capture function remain byte-identical. Additional CTM reads add local observation work; their native cost is not measured here."
  ],
  "independentReview": "favorable",
  "nativeValidationPending": true,
  "limitations": [
    "Source geometry and the synthetic four-case oracle do not replace the next exact-head browser run.",
    "Anchor/isotropy checks establish geometric registration, not pixel-perfect artistic identity of generated views.",
    "The profile and variant angles are authored camera targets, not a measured reconstruction of a canonical 3D hull."
